WEBVTT

00:00:13.830 --> 00:00:15.120
Washimi?

00:00:15.200 --> 00:00:17.330
Washimi!

00:00:18.910 --> 00:00:21.000
You called, sir?

00:00:21.620 --> 00:00:23.910
I wonder if you could
take a look at this.

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:27.660
What's this?

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:31.950
I'm thinking of putting up
an objet d'art-like somen noodle slide

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:34.040
in the office next summer!

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:35.660
This is the model!

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:41.120
The sound of noodles
sliding through water...

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:45.370
I think it could boost our employees'
morale during the hot months.

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:50.200
Rejected.

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:52.450
Don't waste time on such tasks.

00:00:52.540 --> 00:00:54.750
Let me tell you
your schedule for today.

00:00:54.830 --> 00:00:56.120
How cruel!

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:59.200
Our company is very old-fashioned,
so I was trying

00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:02.450
to brighten things up with perks
like the ones at tech companies!

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:05.910
No tech company
has a noodle slide in the office.

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:10.620
Show some respect. You're the secretary!

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:14.700
This model cost 300,000 yen to make!

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:16.830
RECEIPT 300,000 YEN

00:01:18.830 --> 00:01:20.750
Don't tell me...

00:01:21.410 --> 00:01:25.450
Did you plan to put this
on company expenses?

00:01:26.950 --> 00:01:27.910
Can't I?

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:30.700
This is your hobby.

00:01:31.700 --> 00:01:35.040
Wait a second, Ms. Washimi! Please!

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:37.160
Your predecessor would have been upset.

00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:41.330
Wait! Please!

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:42.950
RAGE

00:02:21.200 --> 00:02:23.660
KARAOKE
RECEPTION 2ND FLOOR

00:02:23.750 --> 00:02:26.660
You want to get married
and be a full-time housewife?!

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:31.910
So this is why you started yoga.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:36.200
I see.
In other words...

00:02:36.290 --> 00:02:40.790
You sculpt your body through yoga,
bag a boyfriend who earns good money,

00:02:40.870 --> 00:02:44.450
marry at 26 or 27, quit your job,
and live happily ever after.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:46.250
That's your plan?

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:50.660
Well, I never said
"live happily ever after," but...

00:02:53.330 --> 00:02:55.370
What's wrong?

00:02:55.910 --> 00:02:58.370
There's no one you like now, right?

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:00.950
You just want to run
away from your job.

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:05.910
Don't underestimate housework.
Marriage isn't a walk in the park.

00:03:07.450 --> 00:03:10.700
You'll have zombie-like friends
who are tired of parenting.

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:13.250
Some marriages also
go completely cold.

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:18.160
I pity the husband who's being chosen
out of convenience.

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:20.040
Husbands aren't ATMs, you know.

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:26.580
Gori, stop nodding and say something!

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:29.830
Well, I don't know!

00:03:29.910 --> 00:03:32.160
Marriage isn't entirely a gamble, though!

00:03:32.540 --> 00:03:36.000
Love is a good thing,
regardless of how it starts!

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:40.500
Well, if that's what you think.
Whatever.

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:54.790
<i>Maybe Ms. Washimi is right, and it is</i>
<i>naïve to look for escape in marriage.</i>

00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:57.580
<i>Still...</i>

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:01.330
Hey, short-timer!

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:05.040
Tea! Tea!

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:06.790
Tea! Tea! Tea!

00:04:06.870 --> 00:04:10.660
<i>I could be attacked at any time</i>
<i>and from any side.</i>

00:04:12.080 --> 00:04:14.040
Tea!

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:16.080
<i>His range extends by the day.</i>

00:04:16.580 --> 00:04:19.700
Tea-tea-tea-tea-tea-tea-tea-tea!

00:04:19.790 --> 00:04:23.080
<i>How am I going to survive</i>
<i>this harsh battle?</i>

00:04:24.250 --> 00:04:25.620
-Tea!
-I want one!

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:27.120
-Me too!
-Don't forget me!

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.790
<i>All these guys jumping on board</i>
<i>tick me off!</i>

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:33.950
Fetching tea suits you perfectly,
short-timer.

00:04:37.160 --> 00:04:39.250
TEA ROOM

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:44.790
<i>Maybe I'll add some dishrag water </i>
<i>in the tea.</i>

00:04:46.910 --> 00:04:48.080
<i>Maybe not.</i>

00:04:50.620 --> 00:04:51.620
Here you are.

00:04:55.580 --> 00:04:57.290
Not even a "thank you"!

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:08.580
Director Ton! Thank you
for the treat the other day!

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:10.910
Tsunoda!

00:05:11.370 --> 00:05:13.580
The pleasure was all mine.

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:18.450
Is that a new golf club? Amazing!

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:22.080
You don't miss anything, do you?
I've got a brand new driver!

00:05:22.450 --> 00:05:24.870
I hit an eagle with this baby last week!

00:05:24.950 --> 00:05:29.410
Wow! I don't know what an eagle is
but it sounds amazing!

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.830
It was a dogleg hole.
I was two down from top.

00:05:32.910 --> 00:05:35.580
I hit against the wind over the trees
and took the lead!

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:38.910
Amazing!

00:05:42.790 --> 00:05:46.580
Tsunoda is busy cozying up to him again.

00:05:47.120 --> 00:05:50.580
It is amazing how she can butter him up
without a shred of shame.

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:52.790
Yeah...

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:02.790
I can't believe you
invited me out for dinner.

00:06:03.080 --> 00:06:06.330
Yeah. There's something
I would like to ask you.

00:06:07.040 --> 00:06:10.040
How do you manage to
manipulate him so easily?

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:12.500
-Manipulate?
-Yes. Director Ton.

00:06:12.580 --> 00:06:16.870
I mean, you have him
wrapped around your little finger.

00:06:16.950 --> 00:06:20.870
Oh, stop it!
It's pretty normal.

00:06:21.620 --> 00:06:24.410
I don't know what
"normal" means to you.

00:06:26.410 --> 00:06:30.370
Ms. Retsuko, you don't think
I'm sucking up to him, do you?

00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:33.200
No! Not really!

00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:36.370
It's OK. I am.

00:06:38.790 --> 00:06:42.200
What Director Ton wants to hear is,
put very simply...

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:44.040
"I'm so great!"

00:06:44.120 --> 00:06:45.250
Easy.

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:48.250
That's why I always say to him, "Amazing!"

00:06:48.330 --> 00:06:52.330
If it puts him in a good mood,
why not take advantage of it?

00:06:52.410 --> 00:06:55.870
Same thing as telling girls
that they are cute.

00:06:57.160 --> 00:06:59.910
That's very forthright, isn't it?

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:01.790
Of course it is!

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:05.120
Here is your order.
Sorry about the wait.

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:07.660
But...

00:07:09.120 --> 00:07:12.830
Doesn't it feel like you've surrendered
if you flatter him?

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:17.580
It only feels like you've lost.
So that's not a defeat, is it?

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:19.200
Oh...

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:24.160
People tend to hate me for this, though.

00:07:24.250 --> 00:07:26.250
What? Really?

00:07:26.330 --> 00:07:27.870
Who could hate you?

00:07:28.290 --> 00:07:30.250
Take Ms. Fenneko,

00:07:30.700 --> 00:07:33.080
she really hates me, doesn't she?

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:35.500
Who knows...

00:07:35.580 --> 00:07:38.750
It's fine. I don't really care.

00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:41.750
Let's eat before the food gets cold.

00:07:41.830 --> 00:07:45.040
First I'll take a picture.

00:07:54.540 --> 00:07:55.370
Why?!

00:07:57.250 --> 00:08:01.000
Why is there a picture of Retsuko
being friendly with Tsunoda?

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:05.830
Retsuko! What the heck is going on
with you and Tsunoda?!

00:08:05.910 --> 00:08:08.580
What do you mean? We just dined together.

00:08:08.660 --> 00:08:11.660
Are you crossing to the other side?
Becoming obsessed with your image?

00:08:11.750 --> 00:08:14.790
Hustling for likes online?

00:08:14.870 --> 00:08:16.830
It's nothing like that.

00:08:16.910 --> 00:08:17.950
That's fine, then...

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:19.620
ACCOUNTING DEPARTMENT

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:20.830
Oh, Retsuko.

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:23.790
I fixed your laptop.

00:08:24.160 --> 00:08:26.870
Really? Thank you!

00:08:28.330 --> 00:08:31.620
Amazing! It's really fast now!

00:08:31.700 --> 00:08:34.450
You barely had any space left
on your hard drive.

00:08:34.540 --> 00:08:37.450
I swapped out the drive
and optimized your settings.

00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:40.750
Haida...

00:08:42.700 --> 00:08:44.410
Amazing!

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:46.700
Amazing!

00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:50.580
No big deal.

00:08:50.870 --> 00:08:53.580
I can fix it again anytime you want.

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:57.370
<i>All right!</i>
<i>Successful attempt!</i>

00:08:58.120 --> 00:09:00.750
<i>Next comes the real battle!</i>

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:09.330
Very... busy!

00:09:09.620 --> 00:09:13.950
Very... busy!

00:09:18.950 --> 00:09:21.750
Director Ton!
Are you practicing golf?

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:25.250
That's amazing!

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:27.290
What part?

00:09:30.120 --> 00:09:34.040
Your swing?
I thought it was amazing.

00:09:34.120 --> 00:09:36.160
How is my swing amazing?

00:09:36.250 --> 00:09:39.160
Well... Your hip stance...

00:09:39.250 --> 00:09:40.580
Hip?!

00:09:41.250 --> 00:09:42.370
What's wrong?

00:09:45.160 --> 00:09:48.000
I hurt my back trying to pick up
the chopsticks last night!

00:09:48.370 --> 00:09:52.620
I've tried every trick in the book.
I'm preparing for Saturday's competition.

00:10:00.700 --> 00:10:03.700
I understand. You're making fun of me.

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:05.790
No, no!

00:10:05.870 --> 00:10:07.870
Director, how can I help?

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:09.660
-Rub me!
-Yes, sir!

00:10:10.200 --> 00:10:12.700
Retsuko! People like you...!

00:10:13.040 --> 00:10:14.160
What?!

00:10:14.660 --> 00:10:17.950
<i>Why? Why?</i>

00:10:19.620 --> 00:10:23.620
<i>Why did this happen?!</i>

00:10:29.120 --> 00:10:30.750
How awkward!

00:10:33.700 --> 00:10:36.540
But it's good that you're taking action.

00:10:36.620 --> 00:10:40.500
The girl who gave you that advice
sounds wise.

00:10:40.870 --> 00:10:43.620
Do you butter up men by telling them
 how amazing they are?

00:10:43.700 --> 00:10:48.910
I do. Not lightly, but I'll use it as
a last resort with a man I'm aiming for.

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:50.580
I see...

00:10:50.870 --> 00:10:53.620
In my case, I'm usually
the one being told I'm amazing.

00:10:53.700 --> 00:10:54.580
Oh...

00:10:54.660 --> 00:10:57.870
Recently a youngster told me
that I looked great.

00:10:57.950 --> 00:10:59.290
Oh my...

00:11:00.950 --> 00:11:03.080
I gave it my best shot...

00:11:04.950 --> 00:11:08.500
But I really think my only option
is to get married and quit...

00:11:11.500 --> 00:11:14.370
<i>Look, Director Ton is used to </i>
<i>treating you in a certain way.</i>

00:11:14.910 --> 00:11:18.120
It's impossible
to suddenly change that dynamic.

00:11:18.700 --> 00:11:21.330
It seems that you pushed too hard,
too soon.

00:11:22.330 --> 00:11:24.450
Then what should I do?

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:27.040
You know, adults...

00:11:27.290 --> 00:11:29.450
Once they set their eyes on a prize...

00:11:31.040 --> 00:11:32.620
They get to scheming.

00:11:47.370 --> 00:11:50.830
<i>What is Ms. Washimi up to?</i>

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:53.450
PRESIDENT'S ROOM

00:11:57.660 --> 00:11:58.620
Come in.

00:11:59.120 --> 00:12:00.620
Excuse me.

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:02.700
What is it?

00:12:02.790 --> 00:12:06.750
It's about the reimbursement
of the cost of your model.

00:12:08.290 --> 00:12:12.080
I've taken care of it.

00:12:13.160 --> 00:12:14.750
Oh, really?

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:20.200
Thank you! I have to
tip my hat to you, Washimi.

00:12:20.290 --> 00:12:21.410
By the way, sir...

00:12:21.910 --> 00:12:23.910
I'd like to discuss a separate matter.

00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:27.700
It's about Director Ton in Accounting.

00:12:34.540 --> 00:12:37.290
Wait, I don't really have
anywhere to go to this time.

00:12:43.450 --> 00:12:45.000
Power harassment, you say?

00:12:45.080 --> 00:12:48.750
And troubling reports
of sexual discrimination.

00:12:48.830 --> 00:12:52.370
But it's just a rumor, right?
I would wager that there is no proof.

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:54.830
Is it really that big a deal?

00:12:54.910 --> 00:12:58.330
Some people just whine about anything.

00:13:01.250 --> 00:13:02.370
Sir.

00:13:03.290 --> 00:13:06.290
This poses a risk for the company.

00:13:06.370 --> 00:13:11.290
Ton's behavior is impacting directly
a female employee's mental health.

00:13:11.370 --> 00:13:15.160
What's to stop her from putting this
online or taking it to the media?

00:13:16.620 --> 00:13:20.370
If you want to see the company's name
dragged through the mud,

00:13:20.830 --> 00:13:23.410
please feel free to
ignore this problem.

00:13:27.040 --> 00:13:29.080
I discussed the issue with the president.

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:32.370
Amazing!

00:13:32.450 --> 00:13:35.200
Retsuko, did you bring
that receipt I gave you?

00:13:35.290 --> 00:13:36.790
Ah, yes.

00:13:36.870 --> 00:13:39.330
I haven't finished processing it, though.

00:13:40.370 --> 00:13:41.660
That's okay.

00:13:42.160 --> 00:13:43.540
RECEIPT 300,000 YEN

00:13:45.450 --> 00:13:46.370
What?!

00:13:46.870 --> 00:13:49.790
I never said that
Accounting had accepted it.

00:13:49.870 --> 00:13:53.750
I told him that I had taken care of it.

00:13:53.830 --> 00:13:57.790
That clueless CEO annoyed me,

00:13:57.870 --> 00:14:00.540
rambling about how he
doubted there was proof.

00:14:01.040 --> 00:14:02.540
So this is what he gets.

00:14:03.290 --> 00:14:06.330
Ms. Washimi, I love you!

00:14:12.120 --> 00:14:17.660
So you see, your management style
comes off a little strong at times,

00:14:18.160 --> 00:14:20.500
so I would prefer that you

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:24.450
don't rock the boat unnecessary.

00:14:24.750 --> 00:14:27.290
What would I have to do?

00:14:27.370 --> 00:14:30.080
Get along with everyone.

00:14:30.160 --> 00:14:33.330
Strive to create
a modern work environment.

00:14:33.790 --> 00:14:35.370
That kind of thing?

00:14:43.870 --> 00:14:45.870
Subtitle translation: John Haguewood
